WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.298 --> 00:00:24.035
An hour before sunset in October 1815, a man traveling on foot entered a little town in France.

2
00:00:24.955 --> 00:00:31.768
The few people who were at their windows at that hour nervously watched this wretched-looking traveler.

3
00:00:31.808 --> 00:00:37.551
He wore a coarse yellow shirt, blue trousers with holes in the knees, and a ragged, gray smock

4
00:00:37.611 --> 00:00:40.432
that was patched with green cloth sewed with twine.

5
00:00:41.592 --> 00:00:44.213
His hair was short and his beard was long.

6
00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:50.436
He appeared to be in his mid-forties, although it was difficult to tell because a leather cap hid

7
00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:52.317
part of his sweaty, dusty face.

8
00:00:53.597 --> 00:00:57.979
The man must have been walking all day because he appeared very weary.

9
00:00:58.679 --> 00:01:02.333
When he reached the center of town, he walked toward the mayor's office.

10
00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:06.294
He went in and fifteen minutes later, he came out.

11
00:01:07.115 --> 00:01:10.496
The stranger made his way toward the inn and entered the kitchen.

12
00:01:11.216 --> 00:01:14.718
The innkeeper was busy preparing a huge dinner in the fireplace.

13
00:01:16.378 --> 00:01:22.681
Hearing the door open and a newcomer enter, the innkeeper asked, without raising his eyes, "What does monsieur

14
00:01:22.721 --> 00:01:25.682
want?" "Something to eat and a place to stay."

15
00:01:25.702 --> 00:01:27.063
"Nothing is easier."

16
00:01:27.363 --> 00:01:32.017
The innkeeper looked up and started to smile, but then he saw his ragged guest.

17
00:01:32.037 --> 00:01:33.538
"For pay."

18
00:01:34.458 --> 00:01:37.080
The man drew a large leather purse from his pocket.

19
00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:38.401
"I have money."

20
00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:39.921
"Then I am at your service.

21
00:01:40.002 --> 00:01:40.582
Have a seat."

22
00:01:41.502 --> 00:01:46.505
While the stranger waited for his dinner, the innkeeper scribbled a note and handed it to a boy.

23
00:01:47.326 --> 00:01:49.727
He whispered something to the child, who ran off.

24
00:01:50.387 --> 00:01:54.449
In a few minutes the boy returned and showed a scrap of paper to the innkeeper.

25
00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:58.772
The innkeeper went over to the stranger, who was sitting by the fire.

26
00:01:59.464 --> 00:02:00.145
"Is dinner ready?"

27
00:02:00.505 --> 00:02:01.185
asked the man.

28
00:02:01.205 --> 00:02:02.226
"Get out!"

29
00:02:02.666 --> 00:02:04.327
the innkeeper whispered in his ear.

30
00:02:04.348 --> 00:02:09.811
"I was suspicious when you arrived so I sent a message to the mayor's office.

31
00:02:10.492 --> 00:02:14.514
I know you're Jean Valjean and I also know what you are."

32
00:02:15.495 --> 00:02:19.978
The stranger bowed his head, picked up his knapsack, and went outside.

33
00:02:20.739 --> 00:02:25.982
He walked through the town, stopping to ask for food and lodgings at a tavern and a house,

34
00:02:26.603 --> 00:02:28.064
but no one would let him in.

35
00:02:28.884 --> 00:02:30.805
The weary man even tried the prison.

36
00:02:30.825 --> 00:02:34.467
"A prison isn't a tavern," said the guard at the door.

37
00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:37.109
"Get yourself arrested and we'll open the door for you."

38
00:02:37.969 --> 00:02:42.812
It was now dark, and the exhausted stranger lay on a stone bench in front of the church.

39
00:02:43.513 --> 00:02:46.374
Just then an old woman emerged from the church.

40
00:02:47.215 --> 00:02:48.115
"What are you doing?"

41
00:02:48.415 --> 00:02:48.996
she asked.

42
00:02:49.016 --> 00:02:51.117
"Can't you see I'm going to sleep?"

43
00:02:51.497 --> 00:02:52.378
he said angrily.

44
00:02:52.398 --> 00:02:54.359
"You can't sleep there.

45
00:02:54.919 --> 00:02:55.980
Have you tried the inn?"

46
00:02:57.608 --> 00:03:00.169
"I don't have enough money for the inn," Valjean lied.

47
00:03:00.189 --> 00:03:03.050
"I've knocked on every door, and everybody has driven me away."

48
00:03:03.831 --> 00:03:05.571
The woman handed him four coins.

49
00:03:05.591 --> 00:03:08.893
"Take these and knock on that door over there."

50
00:03:09.433 --> 00:03:11.994
She pointed to a small house next to the church.

51
00:03:13.014 --> 00:03:19.357
Bishop Myriel lived there with his sister, Mademoiselle Baptistine, and their housekeeper, Madame Magloire.

52
00:03:20.057 --> 00:03:23.719
The bishop was famous for giving away most of his wealth to the poor.

53
00:03:24.279 --> 00:03:30.425
The only luxury he allowed himself was to keep some silver: a set of six plates, a ladle,

54
00:03:30.765 --> 00:03:31.886
and two candlesticks.

55
00:03:32.426 --> 00:03:34.166
There were no locks on his doors.

56
00:03:35.426 --> 00:03:40.708
While Madame Magloire was at the market, she heard that a dangerous man had arrived in town.

57
00:03:40.728 --> 00:03:42.928
"He's a dangerous beggar!"

58
00:03:43.369 --> 00:03:47.470
she said breathlessly to Bishop Myriel as he sat before the fire with his sister.

59
00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:53.951
"Everyone is locking their doors, but we don't have locks and you have the bad habit of saying,

60
00:03:53.971 --> 00:04:00.439
‘Come in,' even at midnight and She chattered on about the dangerous man, but the bishop wasn't listening.

61
00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:03.502
Just then there was a violent knock at the door.

62
00:04:03.522 --> 00:04:04.583
"Come in!"

63
00:04:05.043 --> 00:04:05.744
said the bishop.

64
00:04:06.504 --> 00:04:11.749
The door opened wide as if pushed by someone with great strength, and the stranger entered.

65
00:04:12.389 --> 00:04:14.731
Madame Magloire didn't dare to scream.

66
00:04:15.411 --> 00:04:18.434
Mademoiselle Baptistine sat trembling with her mouth open.

67
00:04:19.014 --> 00:04:21.657
Bishop Myriel looked calmly at the intruder.

68
00:04:21.677 --> 00:04:24.419
"My name is Jean Valjean and I'm a convict!"

69
00:04:24.739 --> 00:04:25.600
blurted out the man.

70
00:04:26.356 --> 00:04:28.337
"I spent 19 years on the prison ships.

71
00:04:28.957 --> 00:04:32.279
Four days ago I was set free, and I've walked thirty miles today.

72
00:04:32.679 --> 00:04:33.499
Can I stay here?"

73
00:04:33.519 --> 00:04:37.641
"Madame Magloire, set another place at the table," said the bishop.

74
00:04:37.661 --> 00:04:39.882
"Did you hear me?

75
00:04:39.902 --> 00:04:40.722
I'm a convict!"

76
00:04:41.102 --> 00:04:41.763
said Valjean.

77
00:04:42.203 --> 00:04:43.684
"Here's my yellow identity card.

78
00:04:44.004 --> 00:04:45.965
That's enough to get me kicked out wherever I go!

79
00:04:46.505 --> 00:04:49.466
It says right here: ‘This man is very dangerous.'

80
00:04:50.326 --> 00:04:53.568
I must show it at the mayor's office in every town where I spend the night."

81
00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:56.321
"Monsieur, sit down," said the bishop.

82
00:04:56.341 --> 00:04:59.543
"We'll eat shortly and your bed will be made ready."

83
00:05:00.483 --> 00:05:03.805
Valjean could not believe that someone was treating him so kindly.

84
00:05:04.466 --> 00:05:08.728
He was soon eating from the silver plates with the bishop and Mademoiselle Baptistine.

85
00:05:09.488 --> 00:05:13.350
After dinner the bishop showed him to a bed near the bishop's own bedroom.

86
00:05:14.111 --> 00:05:19.313
As they were passing through the bishop's room, Madame Magloire was putting away the silver in the cupboard

87
00:05:19.373 --> 00:05:20.094
behind the bed.

88
00:05:20.114 --> 00:05:23.856
"A good night's rest will make you feel better," said the bishop.

89
00:05:25.036 --> 00:05:29.139
"Thank you," said Valjean quietly, but then his voice turned harsh.

90
00:05:29.159 --> 00:05:31.161
"You let me sleep so close to you.

91
00:05:31.561 --> 00:05:32.742
How do you know I'm not a murderer?"

92
00:05:33.403 --> 00:05:35.965
The bishop just smiled and said, "Good night."

93
00:05:36.846 --> 00:05:41.549
Although Valjean had told the bishop that he was a convict, he hadn't told the whole story.

94
00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.812
He'd been born into a poor peasant family.

95
00:05:45.393 --> 00:05:48.775
After he grew up, he became a tree pruner like his father.

96
00:05:49.416 --> 00:05:52.018
Valjean's parents had died when he was very young.

97
00:05:52.498 --> 00:05:55.937
He had only one relative left, a sister who took him in.

98
00:05:56.657 --> 00:06:01.901
When her husband died, she had seven children ranging in age from one to eight.

99
00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:07.245
Valjean was then in his mid-twenties and took his place as head of the household.

100
00:06:08.005 --> 00:06:11.207
He earned 18 sous a day during tree-pruning season.

101
00:06:11.768 --> 00:06:15.890
After that season ended, he worked as a reaper, driver, or laborer.

102
00:06:16.911 --> 00:06:18.592
He did whatever work he could find.

103
00:06:19.633 --> 00:06:24.016
His sister also worked, but misery closed in on this sad family.

104
00:06:25.716 --> 00:06:27.337
There was a very severe winter.

105
00:06:27.878 --> 00:06:31.220
Valjean had no work, and the family had nothing to eat.

106
00:06:32.041 --> 00:06:36.344
Valjean broke into a bakery and stole a loaf of bread for the children.

107
00:06:36.984 --> 00:06:39.306
The baker ran after him and caught him.

108
00:06:40.006 --> 00:06:43.649
Valjean was arrested and sentenced to five years on a prison ship.

109
00:06:44.309 --> 00:06:49.152
He was dressed in a red smock, and his past life was erased, even his name.

110
00:06:49.973 --> 00:06:52.335
He was now a prisoner—Number 24601.

111
00:06:54.536 --> 00:06:58.198
His four escape attempts lengthened his sentence to 19 years.

112
00:06:58.999 --> 00:07:03.841
He lost track of his family, although he later heard that his sister and one child had moved

113
00:07:03.881 --> 00:07:04.402
to Paris.

114
00:07:05.082 --> 00:07:10.845
There was one area where Valjean excelled in prison: He was stronger than the other inmates and could

115
00:07:10.905 --> 00:07:13.207
lift and hold enormous weights on his back.

116
00:07:14.067 --> 00:07:21.271
Jean Valjean had walked onto the prison ship sobbing and shuddering, but he left it hardened physically, mentally,

117
00:07:21.871 --> 00:07:22.632
and spiritually.

118
00:07:23.368 --> 00:07:26.013
He was a very dangerous man indeed.
